This script:
1. Adds two more list items to the list (so now we have four).
2. Updates the count to "4 of 4 results".
3. Removes the button that was clicked (the #more button) from the DOM.

The problem: when the #more button is removed, the focus that was on that button is lost. The browser then shifts focus to the body (or the next available focusable element). We see in the state.focus that the focus is on the body.

